{"study_accession":"PRJNA758290","secondary_study_accession":"SRP334510","title":"Genetic variants and cell-specific signatures in PBMCs of pre transplant recipients","description":"Long-term survival of the renal allograft is a challenge. A single cell sequencing analysis is a powerful approach to identify genetic/genomic risk for development of long-term graft loss at single cell level. In this study, we compared single cell RNA sequencing profiles of pre-transplant PBMC samples from 4 transplant patients (2 patients with graft loss within 3 years vs 2 patients without graft loss) with simultaneous genome-wide genotype data for common variants to idenitfy the immune cell subtypes and transcriptomic signatures associated with long-term graft loss. These transcriptomic data also integrates with genetic data in an effort to identify genes that mediate the risk for graft survival in a cell-type specific context. Overall design: 4 PBMC samples: two with graft loss within 3 years and the other two without graft loss","pubmed":"34499625","geo_series":"","n_samples":8,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN21019994","study_accession":"PRJNA758290","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMC-1_S6_L003","description":"PBMC-1_S6_L003","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM5542927","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-09-01","attributes":[["source_name","PBMC"],["graft loss","NO"],["tissue","PBMC"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR15657993","experiment_accession":"SRX11954996","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":285824675,"base_count":25724220750,"first_public":"2021-09-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5542927: PBMC-1_S6_L003 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":true},{"sample_accession":"SAMN21019995","study_accession":"PRJNA758290","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"PBMC-1_S6_L004","description":"PBMC-1_S6_L004","sex":"","geo_sa